The arcane intelligence is a thinking engine at [[Org/Bisney and Dixar/index|Bisney and Dixar]], wired into the studio's databases and set to build films out of old material. Left running overnight, it met one paradox after another, and each time it cast a spell and drew more power to get past them. Past midnight it made a world of its own, and a boom from the studio put out every light in [[Geography/Los Diablos|Los Diablos]] until the city was dark.

The film it made opens on the island of [[Org/Bisney and Dixar/Arcane Intelligence#Afro-China|Afro-China]], where a giant mandrill statue chooses three villains to recover an enchanted mirror stolen by the demigod Maui: [[People/Hades|Hades]], [[People/Fulton|Fulton]] and [[People/Runway Brian|Runway Brian]]. The three came out of the film through the mirror at its end, into the real world.

## Afro-China

Afro-China is the small, isolated island where the film made by the arcane intelligence opens. The spire of Notre Dame rises over it, with a temple to Zeus at its top, and its people keep the Day of Destiny, when the temple's giant mandrill statue chooses the heroes who will save the world. That day it chose three villains, [[People/Hades|Hades]], [[People/Fulton|Fulton]] and [[People/Runway Brian|Runway Brian]], and set them to recover the enchanted mirror the demigod Maui had stolen. Magic on the island stops anyone from teleporting away, and past its shore the world is left unrendered, a blur of color.

## Elephant Graveyard of Wonders

The Elephant Graveyard of Wonders lies in the desert of the Serengeti, in the film made by the arcane intelligence. Elephants come there to die and to hoard their goods, and their bones and treasures fill a cavern under the sand. A giant tiger's head rises from the sand at its gate and asks what the most powerful magic is: true love's kiss, friendship, or an uninterrupted long rest. Within, the genie [[People/Jaskar|Jaskar]] kept the [[Phenomena/Enchanted Mirror|enchanted mirror]] that the demigod Maui hid there.
